@startuml authoring-flow
' The authoring flow, end to end.
'
'   java -jar plantuml.jar -tsvg docs/diagrams/authoring-flow.puml
'
' The one thing this diagram exists to say: every arrow into the corpus
' passes through the review gate, and everything below the corpus is
' regenerated from it. Only the author writes raw/ — with two named
' exceptions, drawn in the author's own colour because that is what makes
' them exceptional.

top to bottom direction

skinparam backgroundColor #dddddd
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Helvetica"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam nodesep 14
skinparam ranksep 26
skinparam ArrowColor #6b739c
skinparam ArrowFontColor #6b739c
skinparam ArrowFontSize 10

skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #dcdfe8
  FontColor #1a1b26
  BackgroundColor #ffffff
  roundCorner 3
}

skinparam package {
  BorderColor #dcdfe8
  FontColor #6b739c
  BackgroundColor transparent
  FontSize 11
}

' Layer colours are litfire's own TUI role colours, from source/theme.ts:
'   author #d2481a · model #7a4bbd · computed #2b5fa8
package "1 · You write" #FDF6F3 {
  rectangle "**Obsidian**\nor any editor" as obsidian #FFF3EE
  rectangle "**/<kind> new**\n**/<kind> edit**" as buffer #FFF3EE
  rectangle "**/questions <kind>**" as interview #FFF3EE
}

package "2 · The only thing you own" #FDF6F3 {
  rectangle "**raw/<kind>/<id>.md**\nfreeform · the filename is the id" as raw #FFEDE5
  rectangle "**raw/interviews/**\ntimestamped transcripts" as transcripts #FFEDE5
}

package "3 · The tool proposes" #F7F4FC {
  rectangle "**/ingest <kind>**\nnotes → pages" as ingest #F2EDFA
  rectangle "**/ingest interview**\none transcript, every kind" as ingestI #F2EDFA
  rectangle "**/ingest adopt**\npage → note · no model" as adopt #F2EDFA
  rectangle "**/curator**\nmay restructure" as curator #F2EDFA
  rectangle "**/reviewer**\nmay only correct prose" as reviewer #F2EDFA
}

package "4 · Nothing lands without a decision" #F3EDFB {
  rectangle "==review gate\none diff at a time · accept · reject · edit" as gate #E8DEF8
}

package "5 · Regenerated, never edited" #F2F5FB {
  rectangle "**corpus**\ncharacters/ · places/ · factions/ · themes/\ntimeline/moments/ · timeline/arcs/ · situations/\n//every page cites the note it came from//" as corpus #E9F0FA
  rectangle "**ledger/**\nreplay" as ledger #E3ECF8
  rectangle "**wiki/**\n/wiki build" as wiki #E3ECF8
  rectangle "**manuscript.md**\n/export" as manuscript #E3ECF8
}

' --- 1 → 2 -----------------------------------------------------------
obsidian --> raw
buffer --> raw
interview --> transcripts

' --- 2 → 3 -----------------------------------------------------------
raw --> ingest : **new** or **changed** only\n//source_hash decides//
transcripts --> ingestI

' --- 3 → 4 -----------------------------------------------------------
ingest --> gate
ingestI --> gate
adopt --> gate
curator --> gate
reviewer --> gate

' --- 4 → 5, and the two ways back into raw ---------------------------
gate --> corpus : accepted
gate -[#d2481a]-> raw : the **only** two writers\nthat are not you

' --- 5 → 5 -----------------------------------------------------------
corpus --> ledger
corpus --> wiki
corpus --> manuscript

note bottom of ledger
  ==Every write path into the computed layer
  · replay, on every load → **ledger/**
  · **/wiki build** → **wiki/**
  · **/export** → **manuscript.md**
  · **/ingest** and **/curator** → **log.md**, append-only

  No proposal can reach any of these. **.litrpg/**,
  **ledger/**, **raw/**, **manuscript.md** and **wiki/** are
  refused by path before their content is read, so
  nothing a model returns can land here at all.

  //Hand edits are lost on the next recompute — which//
  //is the deal, not a defect.//
end note

note bottom of ingest
  Each pass **reads the corpus first**: `/ingest`
  to update rather than duplicate, `/ingest adopt`
  to find the pages with no **source:** yet.
  Not drawn — it would cross every arrow here.
end note

note right of gate
  **P3.** Every write above reaches you as a diff.
  Idempotency is what makes that bearable — an
  unchanged note produces no diffs at all.

  **/ingest** and **/curator** append to **log.md**.
  The other two leave nothing worth recording.
end note

note bottom of raw
  ==Every write path into raw/
  · you, in Obsidian or any editor
  · **/<kind> edit** — the native buffer
  · **/situation cast|place|moment|arc**,
    **/moment at|name**, **/place name**,
    **/arc order|after** — frontmatter only,
    adopting the page first if it is not here yet
  · **/curator** and **/ingest adopt** — the only two
    writers that are not you, and both are gated

  **P6.** None of them touches your prose. A linking
  command sets a field; the body stays yours.

  //resolveInsideVault refuses raw/ to every proposal//
  //unless allowRaw is set. Those two hold it.//
end note

note bottom of corpus
  ==Every write path into the corpus
  Gated — everything a **model** proposes:
  · **/ingest**, **/ingest interview**, **/ingest adopt**
  · **/curator**, **/reviewer**

  Ungated — everything **you** assert directly:
  · **setAuthored**, syncing the page after a linking
    command. A copy of what you just said, not an
    inference about it (D21)
  · **/<kind> new** · **/status write** · **/chapter new|move**
  · **/init**, once, and never over an existing file

  //The gate is for writes the tool authors, not writes//
  //you author. Your own typed edit is already explicit;//
  //asking you to approve it twice would be theatre.//

  Safe to delete **only** once every page cites a
  source. **/ingest adopt** gets a vault there;
  **/lint** says how far it has got.

  //Still open: **/<kind> new** and **/chapter** write here//
  //rather than raw/, and chapters have no raw/ folder//
  //to write to. That is step 4 and an open question.//
end note

@enduml
